{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "At the Airport", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Check Your Ticket ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information involving apologies, thanks, suggestions and invitations in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Letter Y", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">y</span> consonant sound can be difficult to learn. This is because the letter <span class=\"strong\">y</span> can be pronounced as a vowel or a consonant.<br /><br />The letter <span class=\"strong\">y</span> is a consonant when it is the first letter of a syllable that has more than one letter. <br /> <br /> Words like <span class=\"italic\">yes</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">yard</span> and  <span class=\"italic\">you</span> are all examples of  <span class=\"strong\">y</span> as a consonant sound. <br /><br /> Look at the following table to see the difference between <span class=\"strong\">y</span>  as a consonant versus <span class=\"strong\">y</span> as a vowel:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"y\\\" as consonant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"y\\\" as vowel\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yesterday\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"crying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"young\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gym\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "legroom", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the amount of space you have for your legs in an airplane", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There's better food in first class and more legroom.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le09ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in an airport.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "luggage", "type": "name"}, {"content": "suitcase and bags you take on a plane", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You get your luggage first!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le09ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to upgrade ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move to a more expensive seat or area", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I decided to upgrade my ticket.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le09ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "anniversary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a celebration of an important event", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are having their 50th wedding anniversary party this weekend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le09ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to board", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to enter or go onto a plane or ship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sounds like we are boarding.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le09ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn3le09ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Say these words with the <span cl